### Design Rationale Summary:

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| find melon | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task — player must be near melons and facing them |
| find glass | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task — player must approach glass structure and face it |
| mine jukebox | inventory_has | Mine task — mined jukebox drops as item into inventory |
| find beacon | position_near_with_facing | Find/locate task — player must navigate to beacon area and face it |

Key decisions:
- **"find melon"** uses max_distance=5 (tight) since melons are only ~3-4 blocks from spawn — the player essentially just needs to turn and walk a few steps
- **"find glass"** uses max_distance=8 since the glass structure is large and visible from further away
- **"mine jukebox"** uses inventory_has which is the gold standard for mining tasks — no spatial check needed
- **"find beacon"** uses max_distance=8 since the beacon is elevated and behind the glass structure, requiring actual navigation
